# The CRT VOLE tables of FAEST-EM-128f (data)

The matrices of faest-arch-opt's CRT VOLE for `(λ, τ, Δ bits) = (128, 17, 120)`, as produced by its
build (`subprojects/faest-arch-opt/tools/vole_mult_tables.py --preset 128f`, the JSON that
`tools/gen_crt_tables.py` turns into `crt_constants_128f.cpp`), copied verbatim: the JSON's hex
strings, as hex literals (`Nat`s, so that kernel computations on the tables, `Bridge/CrtCheck.lean`,
need no string parsing; the `…Hex` names are the JSON's). Encoding (from the JSON's `semantics`):
every entry is an integer whose bit `i` is component `i` of an `F₂`-vector; a polynomial is its
coefficient vector. `F` (312 rows over `u ∈ F₂¹²⁸`), `G` (312 rows
over `Δ' ∈ F₂¹²⁰`), `W_tree` (128 rows over the 120 tree-residue bits), `W_gate` (128 rows over the
312 gates), `W_crt` (128 rows over `Δ'`).

`Verifier/CrtGen.lean` recomputes `W_crt` and `M_tree` from the moduli, checks the defining
bilinear identity of `F`, `G`, `W_tree`, `W_gate`, and builds the verifier's row tables.
-/

